#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:85
msgid ""
"A tool counts as present when its executable is on ``PATH`` or its "
"configuration directory exists. Without a tool argument, or with "
"``--all``, the command wires every supported tool that is present and "
"reports the others as not installed. A tool that is named explicitly is "
"wired even when it is not detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:92
msgid "Claude Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:94
msgid ""
"The server is registered in the user scope, which applies to every "
"project on the machine. When ``claude`` is on ``PATH`` the entry is "
"created with ``claude mcp add -s user``, because Claude Code manages the "
"locking and the format of its own file. When ``claude`` is not on "
"``PATH`` the command edits ``~/.claude.json`` directly. The operating "
"guide is installed as a skill; it is loaded when a task mentions ANet, "
"and it does not occupy the context of other sessions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:103
msgid "Codex"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:105
msgid ""
"The entry is written inside a block delimited by marker comments. The "
"values ``startup_timeout_sec = 30`` and ``tool_timeout_sec = 900`` are "
"set explicitly: the tool ``wait_task`` blocks until a task changes state,"
" and a task of a remote agent is measured in minutes, whereas the default"
" tool timeout of Codex is 60 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:112
msgid "Cursor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:114
msgid ""
"The entry is written to ``~/.cursor/mcp.json``, which is read by the "
"editor and by ``cursor-agent``. Cursor has no user-level rules file, so "
"no operating guide is installed. An older rule file written by a previous"
" release under ``~/.cursor/rules`` is removed when its content identifies"
" it as ANet's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:121
msgid "opencode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:123
msgid ""
"The entry uses the opencode form, with ``\"type\": \"local\"``, the "
"command and its argument in one array, an explicit ``enabled`` flag, and "
"``environment`` in place of ``env``. When only ``opencode.jsonc`` exists,"
" that file is the target. The editor does not preserve comments: if the "
"file contains comments, the command makes no change and prints the entry "
"for manual insertion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:131
msgid "Hermes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:133
msgid ""
"The entry runs the binary directly. Hermes disables an MCP entry that "
"starts a shell interpreter, so a wrapper such as ``sh -c \"anet mcp\"`` "
"is not used. The timeouts are ``timeout: 900`` and ``connect_timeout: "
"30``. Optional ``a2a_agents`` entries are described in :ref:`howto-"
"coding-agents-hermes-a2a`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:140
msgid "Wiring and unwiring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:143
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:151
msgid ""
"``--all`` and explicit tool names are mutually exclusive. ``--refresh`` "
"and ``--a2a`` apply to Hermes; ``--refresh`` is accepted by ``wire`` "
"only. The command exits with a non-zero status when at least one tool "
"ended in a conflict or an error, so that an installer cannot report "
"success after a partial result."
msgstr ""

