msgid ""
"Restart the coding agent, or start a new session. The tools are loaded at"
" the start of a session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:182
msgid "Check the result:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:188
msgid ""
"The command reports one state for each tool: not installed, not wired, "
"wired and current, wired but outdated (the entry or the guide differs "
"from what ``wire`` would write now), or conflict. For an outdated entry "
"the report names the command that corrects it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:193
msgid ""
"In the coding agent, request the tool ``node_status``. A response that "
"contains the AID and the version of the node confirms that the chain from"
" the agent to the daemon works. If the daemon is not running, the MCP "
"server does not start; the client reports a failed connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:198
msgid "Removal is symmetric:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:205
msgid ""
"``unwire`` removes the MCP entry, the operating guide, and every "
"``a2a_agents`` entry together with its token. An entry with the name "
"``anet`` that ANet did not write is left unchanged and reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:211
msgid "Rules that apply to every change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:213
msgid ""
"The command edits configuration files of other programs. The same rules "
"apply to every tool:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:216
msgid "Backup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:217
msgid ""
"Before a file is changed it is copied to ``<name>.anet-bak-<UTC time>`` "
"next to the original. An existing backup is never overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:220
msgid "Absolute binary path and pinned identity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:221
msgid ""
"The entry names the ``anet`` binary by absolute path and sets "
"``ANET_DATA_DIR`` to the data directory of the identity that was selected"
" when the command ran. An MCP client does not load the shell profile of "
"the operator, and ``anet mcp`` resolves strictly once an identity is "
"pinned: it reaches the daemon of that identity and no other. To wire "
"another identity, select it with ``--id``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:232
msgid ""
"A tool has one ``anet`` entry; a later ``wire`` for another identity "
"replaces the entry written earlier. A binary started through ``go run`` "
"is refused, because the temporary build directory disappears when the "
"process exits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:237
msgid "Atomic writes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:238
msgid ""
"A file is written to a sibling temporary file and renamed. The mode of "
"the replaced file is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:241
msgid "Idempotence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:242
msgid ""
"Running ``wire`` twice changes nothing the second time. After an upgrade "
"of ``anet``, running it again updates the operating guide and, where the "
"binary path changed, the entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:246
msgid "Conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:247
msgid ""
"An existing entry with the name ``anet`` whose command is not ``anet "
"mcp`` is not overwritten. The tool is reported as a conflict, nothing is "
"changed for that tool, and the exit status is non-zero. The conflicting "
"entry is removed or renamed by the operator, and ``wire`` is run again. "
"The same applies to a table ``mcp_servers.anet`` in a Codex file that was"
" not written by ``anet agents wire``; the report gives the line number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:254
msgid "Managed blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:255
msgid ""
"In TOML, YAML and Markdown files the command edits only the text between "
"its own marker lines. Edits inside a managed block are overwritten by the"
" next ``wire``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:259
msgid "Superseded content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/coding-agents.rst:260
msgid ""
"Earlier releases appended a persona block to ``~/.claude/CLAUDE.md``, "
"wrote a rule file under ``~/.cursor/rules``, and, through ``anet install "
"--agent openclaw``, appended a block to ``~/.openclaw/AGENTS.md``. "
"``wire`` removes the Claude Code block and the Cursor file; ``wire "
"--all`` and ``unwire --all`` remove the OpenClaw block when it is "
"present. OpenClaw is not a supported tool."
msgstr ""

